#Security & Best Practices Implemented
Non-Root User: Switched runtime process user from root to node (USER node) to prevent privilege escalation vulnerabilities.

Alpine Base Image: Utilized node:20-alpine to maintain a ultra-minimal OS footprint with fewer installed system packages.

Layer Caching Optimization: Structured COPY package*.json ./ prior to application code so npm ci layer is cached unless dependencies change.

Environment Isolation: Explicitly set ENV NODE_ENV=production to trigger production optimizations in Express and dependency modules.

Clean .dockerignore: Excluded .git, node_modules, npm-debug.log, and environment files from being copied into the build context.


